  "summary": "Four studies directly apply transformer-based self-attention encoder models to battery remaining life estimation, and one additional study applies decentralised training to the same topic. [V0077] (El-Sayed et al., 2022) evaluates self-attention encoders on the CellLife dataset, achieving AUROC 0.87. [V0080] (Haddad et al., 2025) applies self-attention encoders to ProtMap, reporting MAE 0.73. [V0079] (Gupta et al., 2024) uses self-attention encoders on GridWatch, obtaining accuracy 0.66. [V0078] (Fischer et al., 2023) applies self-attention encoders to ToxiBench, achieving F1 0.94. [V0084] (Adebayo et al., 2026) applies decentralised training (not a transformer method) to battery remaining life on ProtMap with AUROC 0.84; it is included as the fifth-ranked document because it addresses the battery health topic, though its method is not transformer-based. Documents applying transformers to unrelated topics (e.g., sepsis, customer attrition, wildfire) are excluded as not directly relevant.",
